{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/897-asia-ascendant","id":897,"title":"Asia Ascendant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T21:28:34-07:00","id":897,"title":"Asia Ascendant","content":"Given its quasi-official status I wonder how much of its content will make it into Trinity 2.0. It seems to me that AsAs was angling the line in the more cossover friendly direction 2.0 sounds to be headed, and I loved the addition of the cyberware and the genetic modification stuff. Though the addition of sci-fi gene mod stuff did create a bit of confusion at my table for new players. I suddenly had to explain the difference between noetic biotech, and more traditional biotech like gene mods. All that said, I think AsAs had a lot of good ideas (if an overly utopian depiction of China that didn't quite mesh with earlier descriptions), and I hope most of it stays in play.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T03:16:48-07:00","id":1019,"title":"","content":"The section on tech was about the only thing I cared for in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T23:57:47-07:00","id":1565,"title":"","content":"I'm still very fond of the Asia Ascendant and I'm the Aeon developer, so make of that what you will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for tech, cybertech and non-noetic bio-mods will both exist and low level ones won't be all that uncommon. However, I've also decided that part of the Aberrant War involved Aberrants taking control of millions of people who had neural jacks, there will also be restrictions on some tech in the setting as well as a pervasive attitude that (especially not that the Aberrants are back) using certain sorts of tech is essentially suicidal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T20:34:19-08:00","id":2326,"title":"","content":"Great news, I always felt official rules for cyber tech were lacking in the original material. And, on a more personal note, that new plot point about the neural jacks works bizarrely well with some things going on in the game I'm currently running. Glad to see some old familiar like you and Ian involved with the resurrection of Trinity.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T20:45:01-08:00","id":2335,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the neural jack as well as the low level non-noetic biotech. I already have made changes in the current series I'm running that added some cyber tech, but it is not as well done as I would like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:48:31-08:00","id":2376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/897-asia-ascendant?p=2335#post2335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the neural jack as well as the low level non-noetic biotech. I already have made changes in the current series I'm running that added some cyber tech, but it is not as well done as I would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad. My take on the TU after the Aberrant War is that just before the Aberrant War, humanity was headed down the path to a radical transhumanist future - in large part because in the hands of the Novas, science &amp; technology was became significantly more impressive every few years. After the Aberrant War, there were no more Aberrants to move things forward and humans ceased trusting any science or technology they couldn't fully understand. Also, technologies that were used by Aberrants to turn people into puppets fell seriously out of fashion, as did anything that made people look significantly non-human (with one exception that I'm including in the core book). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}